DRAWING_CONVENTIONS = """
## BUILDING DRAWING CONVENTIONS - VIETNAMESE & INTERNATIONAL STANDARDS

### GRID SYSTEMS
- Grid lines are long dashed lines (centerlines) labeled with numbers (1,2,3...) horizontally
  and letters (A,B,C...) or numbers vertically
- Grid intersections define column positions
- Typical residential spacing: 3-6m apart
- Typical commercial/industrial spacing: 6-12m apart
- Grid bubbles are circles at line ends containing labels

### STRUCTURAL ELEMENTS
- COLUMNS: Solid filled or hatched rectangles at grid intersections
  - RC column sizes: 200x200 to 600x600mm typical
  - Steel columns: marked with section labels (e.g., H200x200, UB305)
- BEAMS: Lines connecting columns along grid axes
  - RC beams: typically rectangular cross-section, depth = span/8 to span/12
  - Steel beams: I-beam shapes, labeled UB, UC, W, H sections
- SLABS: Indicated by hatch patterns or diagonal text (e.g., S1, S2)
  - Thickness: 100-250mm RC typical

### ARCHITECTURAL ELEMENTS
- WALLS: Double parallel lines on plans; thickness 100-300mm
  - Solid fill = concrete/brick wall
  - Diagonal hatch = block wall
- DOORS: Arc line showing swing direction + gap in wall
  - Single swing: quarter-circle arc
  - Double swing: two symmetric arcs
  - Sliding: arrow in wall gap
  - Standard width: 800-1200mm; height: 2100-2400mm
- WINDOWS: Thin rectangles breaking wall lines
  - Often labeled with dimensions (e.g., W1200x1500)
  - Sill height: 900-1200mm from floor
- STAIRS: Parallel lines with arrow indicating up direction
  - Straight: rectangular block with parallel lines
  - L-shaped/U-shaped: multiple rectangular blocks
  - Circular: curved parallel lines
  - Riser: 150-175mm; Tread: 250-300mm

### DIMENSION CONVENTIONS
- Dimension lines have tick marks or arrows at ends
- Numbers along dimension lines show mm or cm
- Chain dimensions show cumulative distances
- Grid-to-grid dimensions are primary references

### FLOOR LEVELS
- Each floor plan page represents one level
- Floor elevation marks: +0.000 (ground), +3.500 (1st floor), etc.
- Floor height: 3000-4500mm typical residential; 3500-5000mm typical commercial
- Stair annotations often indicate floor levels

### SCALE
- Common architectural scales: 1:50, 1:100, 1:200
- Common structural scales: 1:50, 1:100
- Scale bar is often present on drawings
"""


